{%- comment -%}
  HIVOLT — feed title resolver (G6)

  Shopping feeds and the storefront want different titles. Feeds reward literal,
  front-loaded titles ("HIVOLT Pique Polo Shirt - Men's - Black - M"); a premium
  PDP wants the brand's own naming. Rather than degrade one for the other, the
  feed title lives in its own field and this snippet resolves it.

  Params
    product  required
    variant  optional — when given, variant attributes are appended, which is
                        what an item-level feed row needs
    format   'plain' (default) — the resolved title
             'source'          — 'metafield' or 'fallback', for the audit view

  Fallback is deliberate: with no feed title set, the storefront title is used
  unchanged. That is a valid feed title, not a missing value.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign hv_feed_title = product.metafields.custom.feed_title.value | default: '' | strip
  assign hv_source = 'metafield'
  if hv_feed_title == ''
    assign hv_feed_title = product.title
    assign hv_source = 'fallback'
  endif

  assign hv_suffix = ''
  if variant != blank and product.has_only_default_variant == false
    for hv_option in variant.options
      assign hv_suffix = hv_suffix | append: ' - ' | append: hv_option
    endfor
  endif

  assign hv_resolved = hv_feed_title | append: hv_suffix | strip

  comment
    Merchant Center truncates titles at 150 characters. Truncating here means
    the important words are the ones we chose, not the ones that happened to
    survive.
  endcomment
  assign hv_resolved = hv_resolved | truncate: 150, ''
-%}

{%- if format == 'source' -%}
  {{- hv_source -}}
{%- else -%}
  {{- hv_resolved -}}
{%- endif -%}
